WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:13.139
In this lesson, you will learn to tell the difference between repeating a set number of times and forever, and choose the right loop for a game.

2
00:00:13.739 --> 00:00:17.148
Repeat 3 stops after 3 times.

3
00:00:17.748 --> 00:00:23.330
The red “repeat forever” block keeps going until you press stop.

4
00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:30.383
Things that never stop in a game: clouds floating, fish swimming, music playing.

5
00:00:30.983 --> 00:00:36.130
Things that happen a few times: 3 jumps, 5 steps.

6
00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:42.313
The kangaroo hops exactly 5 times. Use 🔁 with a number.

7
00:00:42.313 --> 00:00:47.461
Exactly 5 — a number loop stops when it’s done.

8
00:00:48.061 --> 00:00:51.904
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

9
00:00:51.904 --> 00:00:57.052
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
